# Go conventions

Match existing package style. See [architecture.md](../../_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture.md) §4.

## Naming

- Exported types: `CamelCase`; packages: single lowercase word
- DB columns and JSON tags: `snake_case`

## Errors

- Wrap with `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)`
- User-visible strings separate from error wrapping (Fyne dialogs vs `slog`)

## Tests

- Table-driven unit tests; temp dir + SQLite for integration
- Name tests with story/NFR IDs when scoped (`TestStory210_*`, `TestNFR01*`)
- Extend the closest existing `*_test.go` — do not duplicate HTTP scenarios outside `internal/share/http_test.go`

## Logging

- Use `log/slog` structured logging
